From 319d4ae5051813149bc0953328dc211d86cdab95 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 05:31:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07207/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-25: wire the
 dynamics-side refactor loop into the stall path -- fires correctly, but net
 effect is null (repair round fails to generate)

_induce_and_plan() gained a DEV-ONLY CARNOT_ARC_STALL_REFACTOR_LOOP=1
branch routing stall-triggered (first-contact) induction through
execute_bounded_llm_reinduction -- previously reachable only from the
level_up_reinduction branch (REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-24). Unset in production,
byte-identical default, verified by a test that fails if the function is
called when unset; a second test confirms the enabled path threads
previous_level_complete_grid=None / structural_goal_provider=None
correctly.

Live re-run on g50t, budget=250, at the k=8 default (isolated from
REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-23's k=20 change). Both arms: stall_refactor_loop_used=
True, refinement_rounds_used=2 -- the mechanism fires correctly. Round 1
(induce) gets partial real signal (5/25 correct baseline, 0/25 sge) but
is correctly rejected by the strict min_heldout_accuracy=1.0 gate. Round
2 (refactor) FAILS to produce parseable code for BOTH arms -- "local
model code unusable after 3 tries" -- so the mechanism's core repair
value-add never executes. planned=False both arms, no improvement over
the k=8 no-refactor baseline.

Notable side-observation: round 1's induced code is qualitatively the
best-reasoned generation this whole REQ chain has seen (dynamic
player-finding by color, general relative-offset movement, a
non-degenerate win predicate) -- but this is attributable to LLM
sampling variance on the plain induce() call, not the refactor loop
itself. Strengthens, rather than refutes, REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-23's
high-variance finding.

